Game of Life on two nodes over TCP on loopback, benchmarks/life/life_two.m,
on small grids: the halves' cells together must be life.m's, with an even
split, an odd one, and halves of one and two rows. Sequentially, and with
OpenMP on the host, where the target regions that exchange the rows run
there, each at -O0 and -O2. The populations and checksums are from an
independent program in Python.

RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/life/life_two.m -o %t.sequential0
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.sequential0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EVEN
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/life/life_two.m -o %t.sequential2
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EVEN
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=301 LIFE_STEPS=17 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=10 LIFE_STEPS=4 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TEN
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=3 LIFE_STEPS=2 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=THREE
RUN: merkc -O0 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life_two.m -o %t.host0
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=301 LIFE_STEPS=17 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.host0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life_two.m -o %t.host2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EVEN
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=301 LIFE_STEPS=17 %python %S/../../benchmarks/life/pair.py %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
REQUIRES: libomp

EVEN: Game of Life, Mercury, two nodes
EVEN-NEXT: Grid: 300 x 300 cells, 8 bytes a cell
EVEN-NEXT: Steps: 25
EVEN-NEXT: Population: 9339
EVEN-NEXT: Checksum: 429141631
